/* Cascading marker-species opts. If the row's Fossil_Group resolves to
   one of MARKER_SPECIES_BY_GROUP, return those species; if it doesn't
   match (or is empty) fall back to a unioned list across all groups —
   so the dropdown is always useful. Adds existing in-state values too,
   so the user's prior typing also surfaces. The column is T.vocab so
   custom species names are still typeable. */
/* ---------- Standard biozonation schemes ----------
   Curated zone names from canonical zonation schemes. The dropdown for
   Biostrat → Zone cascades from the row's Fossil_Group, just like
   Marker_Species does. Lists prioritize widely-used schemes and stay
   short enough to be practical (the popup caps at 200 anyway). User-
   typed values still appear via the live-vocab fallback.

   Sources:
     • Calcareous nannofossils — Martini (1971) NN/NP zones; supplemented
       by Berggren et al. (1995) Cenozoic refinements.
     • Planktonic foraminifera — Berggren & Pearson (2005) PT/PE/PL/E/M;
       Mesozoic from Caron (1985), Robaszynski (2000).
     • Conodonts — Cenozoic and Paleozoic standards (Sweet 1988).
     • Dinoflagellates — Powell (1992), Williams et al. (2004) cosmopolitan.
     • Ammonites — European/Boreal Mesozoic standard chronozones
       (Page 1996, Hardenbol 1998).
     • Pollen / palynomorphs — selected NW European, NA reference zones.
   Lists are illustrative, not exhaustive. */
